[38;5;231m●[39m Terminal width is the number of
  character columns a terminal (or tmux
  pane) can display on one line, so any
  composer text longer than that gets
  hard-wrapped into additional visual
  rows — which is why a single logical
  prompt can appear as multiple lines
  when captured.

  Ready for the regression test plan
  whenever you are.

